US-055 is not complete, so I have not emitted the COMPLETE signal. The Lua API is implemented and every gate that can run on this host passes. The one open acceptance gate is `linux-gcc`, and this machine cannot run it.

**Why the tree needs no new work:** The implementation is in `engine/script/` (the `engine_script` module, a Lua 5.4.7 VM with six globals: `entity`, `transform`, `input`, `assets`, `physics`, `events`), with 15 unit cases in `tests/src/script_lua_tests.cpp`. The latest progress entry records the results. No file under `engine/`, `tests/`, `cmake/`, or `docs/` is newer than that entry, so nothing has changed since it was verified.

**Gate status:**
- Passing on Linux: `ValidateVendor`, `linux-dev`, `linux-debug`, `linux-unit`, `linux-asan` build, and `linux-sanitize`.
- Passing on Windows: `ValidateVendor`, `win-dev`, `win-debug` build, and `win-unit`, per the earlier batch run recorded in progress.
- Not run: `linux-gcc`, `linux-gcc-debug`, and `linux-gcc-unit`. The host has only g++ 9.4, and Jolt needs GCC 11 or newer. `sudo` requires a password here, so I could not install a newer compiler. This gate needs the CI job or a machine with GCC 11+.
- Not run: `engine_bench`, because the benchmark harness is US-074. GPU suites were not run because this story has no GPU work.

**What I did not do this pass:** I did not re-run the gates, since the last recorded pass already covers an unchanged tree. I also did not append another progress entry, because the previous passes already left several identical re-check entries.

**Known gaps, deliberately left for later stories:** scripts have no instruction or time limit, so `while true do end` blocks its thread. There is no component table beyond `transform`, no physics body creation from Lua, and no lifecycle callbacks or reload (US-056).
